# Bump this number to invalidate every Go build cache in hooks.yml.
#
# The cache key is otherwise go.sum/go.mod-only, and a key that never changes is a cache
# that never refreshes: setup-go skips the save on a primary-key hit, so whatever landed
# first stays until a dependency moves. That is survivable when each job saves its OWN
# complete cache (they do now — the keys are per job), and it is not survivable if a bad
# save gets in. This file is the deliberate escape hatch for that case.
#
# It replaces hooks.yml in the key, which was doing this job by accident and charging for
# it: every edit to the workflow — every CI experiment, every comment fix — invalidated all
# nine jobs at once and made each one rebuild the standard library from scratch. Measured
# 2026-08-25 while tuning this file: ~150s per platform per job, and 3m54s for a cold vet
# job that costs ~30s warm. Invalidation should be an act, not a side effect.
1
